# 02-expressions.nez — operators and evaluation order
#
# Nezha's infix grammar is deliberately flat: infix operations evaluate from
# left to right unless parentheses change the grouping. This file also realizes
# every BINOP terminal and both unary operators. `and` and `or` are lazy.
println("== expressions ==")

# Arithmetic operators: + - * /
println(8 + 2)
println(8 - 2)
println(8 * 2)
println(8 / 2)

# Comparison operators: < > <= >=
println(1 < 2)
println(2 > 1)
println(2 <= 2)
println(2 >= 2)

# Flat infix evaluation: (1 + 2) * 3 = 9, not conventional-precedence 7.
println(1 + 2 * 3)

# Grouping makes the intended grouping explicit.
println(1 + (2 * 3))

# Unary negation and logical not.
println(-5)
println(not true)

# `and` and `or` short-circuit; the divisions on the right are never evaluated.
println(false and (1 / 0))
println(true or (1 / 0))
